<p class="patterns-lead">The filters of <code>{pad:open/}image:thumbnail{pad:close/}</code> - each a file of
<code>pad/subs/images/filters/types/</code> in the engine, named in <code>filter=</code>, a comma list applied
in the order written. The picture is made once with GD and kept in <code>_thumbs/</code> like any
thumbnail, the filter and its options part of its name. halftone and ascii write the picture another
way; blurhash, thumbhash, dominant and lqip are placeholders - shown here with the picture made transparent, so
what stands behind it while it loads is what you see.</p>

{array:filters}
<section class="patterns-filter" id="{$filter}">
  <h2>{$filter}</h2>
  <p>{$line}</p>
  <div class="patterns-play{pad:if $behind} patterns-behind{/pad:if}">
    {pad:echo $template | code/}
  </div>
  <pre class="patterns-source"><code>{!source}</code></pre>
</section>
{/array:filters}
